ion  and in fact Abbott Laboratories was one  of the most important private  co-sponsors of war art Abbott's most  important project was arguably Thomas  Hart Benton swell known series the year  of peril painted in 1942 Benton's  canvases including starry night are  filled with violence suffering and with  the art historic an art historian Erica  das has called pseudo surrealism  although intended for government  distribution officials labeled the  series too intense despite criticism  from government officials and art  critics that such unrestrained violence  was counterproductive to the war effort  Benton series was seen widely in  newsreels and in a lavish full-color  brochure sponsored by Abbott and that's  the cover of that brochure on the Left  determining why government officials  would accept one image and reject  another involves multiple factors in  closing it seems more important to note  simply that blooms scene of nautical  suffering was one example of many  created during the war and that this and  similar images projected an unsettling  strange visual experience that offered  viewers an alternative form of realism  than the photographic horrors of war  seen in newspapers magazines and  newsreels the appeal of a month more  unorthodox unpredictable system of magic  realism during this era is in many ways  not surprising after all wartime  anxieties touched countless domestic  economic and cultural standards as  millions of men enlisted and shipped out  overseas preconceived notions regarding  the rules of women and minorities in  public and private life were challenged  upset and reworked these resulting  shifts many of which were sudden and  extreme likely let it likely led many  Americans to see parallels between  wartime culture and the visual  instability of blooms grotesque realism  the suppression of blooms painting  reveals the politicized bureaucracy that  oversaw US government propaganda during  World  or two in fact blooms work was only one  